    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "When you create an owner, the response now includes `capacityWarning: true` if their city already had 40\u201349 owners. Creating an owner in a city that already has 50 is still rejected as before. All 28 tests pass, including the new acceptance test (`./mvnw test`, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\nI copied how the existing `bulkSignupWarning` flag works:\n\n- **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`): the city count is now fetched once and used for both the 50-owner rejection and the warning. The 40 threshold is a new constant, `CITY_CAPACITY_WARNING_THRESHOLD`, next to `CITY_CAPACITY`.\n- **Saved with the owner:** the flag is worked out when the owner is created and stored in a new `capacity_warning` column. Reading the owner back later returns the value from creation time, even if the city fills up afterwards. This change touched:\n  - the `Owner` entity\n  - the schema files for all four databases (H2, HSQLDB, MySQL, Postgres)\n  - the plain-JDBC repository's queries\n- **API:** I added `capacityWarning` to `openapi.yml`, which generates `OwnerDto`, and mapped it in `OwnerMapper`. Owners saved before this change will show `false`.\n\nExisting databases won't pick up the new column on their own. If you run against a MySQL or Postgres instance that already has the `owners` table, you'll need to add `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` to it by hand.",
